[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Object-Oriented Programming (OOPs) Principles in Automation Testing"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Object-Oriented Programming (OOPs) is a fundamental programming paradigm that helps developers and automation engineers structure their code into reusable, modular, and maintainable components. In automation testing, applying OOPs principles significantly reduces code duplication and simplifies framework maintenance."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Encapsulation"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Encapsulation involves bundling the data (variables) and methods (functions) that operate on the data within a single unit, usually a class, and restricting direct access to some of the object's components. In the context of the Page Object Model (POM), private locators are exposed through public getter methods."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"public class LoginPage {
    private By usernameField = By.id("username");
    private By passwordField = By.id("password");
    private By loginButton = By.id("submit");

    public void enterUsername(String user) {
        driver.findElement(usernameField).sendKeys(user);
    }

    public void enterPassword(String pwd) {
        driver.findElement(passwordField).sendKeys(pwd);
    }

    public void clickLogin() {
        driver.findElement(loginButton).click();
    }
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Inheritance"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Inheritance allows a new class to adopt the properties and methods of an existing class. In automation frameworks, a BaseTest class is commonly created to handle common setup and teardown tasks (like initializing the WebDriver or managing configurations), which are then inherited by all test classes."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"public class BaseTest {
    protected WebDriver driver;

    @BeforeMethod
    public void setUp() {
        driver = new ChromeDriver();
        driver.manage().window().maximize();
    }

    @AfterMethod
    public void tearDown() {
        if (driver != null) {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}

public class LoginTest extends BaseTest {
    @Test
    public void testValidLogin() {
        driver.get("https://example.com/login");
        // Test implementation goes here
    }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Polymorphism"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Polymorphism allows objects to be treated as instances of their parent class rather than their actual class. Method overloading (compile-time) and method overriding (run-time) are frequently used in automation to create flexible wrappers around generic actions like explicit waits or element interactions."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"public class ElementActions {
    // Method Overloading
    public void click(By locator) {
        driver.findElement(locator).click();
    }

    public void click(WebElement element) {
        element.click();
    }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Abstraction"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Abstraction hides complex implementation details and exposes only the essential features of an object. In test automation, abstract classes or interfaces define a blueprint for page actions or test configurations, forcing child classes to implement specific methods."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"public interface TestLifecycle {
    void initializeTest();
    void executeTestSteps();
    void cleanupTest();
}

public abstract class BasePage implements TestLifecycle {
    public abstract void verifyPageLoaded();
}"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Applying OOPs in Test Automation"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always keep page locators private and provide public modifier methods for interaction (Encapsulation)."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use a Base class for shared driver initialization and common assertions to prevent redundant code (Inheritance)."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Design custom wrapper functions for logging, reporting, and driver actions using method overloading (Polymorphism)."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Utilize interfaces to standardize the architecture of your automation framework (Abstraction)."}]
